{
  "schema_version": "reader_readiness_manuscript_v18",
  "title": "From Source Availability to Reader Readiness",
  "subtitle": "WikiGraphRAG v18: a research preparation update",
  "date": "4 October 2026",
  "status": "completed_preparation_checkpoint",
  "claims_scope": {
    "novelty": false,
    "natural_qa_gain": false,
    "full_xbrl_conformance": false,
    "generally_strong_reader": false,
    "browser_fidelity_verified": false
  },
  "abstract": "This update separates source inspection, candidate representation and executable reading as prerequisites for an evidence-reader study. Additional views and literal cover identities now have qualified admission. A versioned interface retains blank blocks and original source projections. After an initial observability failure, a logging-only follow-up observes zero rollback state and tokenizes all authored requests. No answers or natural-question results are produced; complete semantic evidence, reader competence, QA gains and retrieval novelty remain unestablished.",
  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "1. Source views and candidate representation",
      "paragraphs": [
        "Reviewers inspected additional whole blocks and caption rows against source and CSS records. Their disjoint model-role assignments are not human annotation or an agreement study. Office-rendered views remain qualified inspection aids with disclosed border and browser-fidelity limits. Separate caption recovery clears a missing-view condition, not semantic attachment.",
        "The interface amendment permits empty or whitespace source blocks only. Witness, label and required aspect text remain nonempty. The shape-only successor uses the same assembly and projection helpers and compares each source-only projection, registry and dependency plan with its frozen parent before writing. All original machine bindings retain their declared-metadata status."
      ],
      "tables": [
        "preparation"
      ],
      "after_tables": [
        "Frozen v16 replay preserves ten passes and eleven blank-text failures. All eight exact parent-comparison categories pass for each successor. Forty dependencies, nineteen blank exposures and 326 bundle occurrence entries remain; the last is not a unique-occurrence audit. The shape-only outputs retain null identity cards and populations. Shape validity establishes neither complete evidence nor answerability."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "2. From loading failure to authored tokenization",
      "page_break_before": true,
      "paragraphs": [
        "The new application policy retains the kernel hard cap, owned-process-group RSS limit, pressure proxy and reserve, address-space limit, time limits and OOM-event stops. It relaxes the former total-boundary stop (current >= max): reaching the total-memory boundary and increasing max events are recorded diagnostically. This is a real policy change with shared-cgroup risk, not proof of fit or equivalent isolation.",
        "The first v18 attempt reaches loaded health and identity responses, then fails closed because its required rollback-state log field is unobserved. That is not evidence of nonzero state. Pinned-source diagnosis identifies suppressed runtime log messages. A separately reviewed follow-up changes logging verbosity only, retaining the same assets, authored requests and limits; it observes zero rollback state and tokenizes every authored request. Both attempts confirm cleanup."
      ],
      "tables": [
        "native_attempt",
        "native_resources"
      ],
      "after_tables": [
        "The follow-up also observes rounded runtime buffer reports, which are not exact allocator-byte measurements or proof of a complete generation working set. Server-default generation settings in props and configured future per-completion settings remain unexercised: no generation request or natural prompt was sent. Different shared resource states preclude an efficiency comparison between attempts."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "3. Semantic readiness and the next scientific gate",
      "page_break_before": true,
      "paragraphs": [
        "A separate source-only review covers every fixed candidate bundle and retains unknowns for currency identity, exact duration, population, entity, beginning balances and unlabeled row concepts. The review has no typed-record access or private numerical registry join; prior public inventory-candidate metadata exposure is disclosed. Its partial source-visible candidates are not human gold or complete semantic maps.",
        "The initial snapshot treats unresolved codes as descriptions within the fixed source-only projection, not universal reasons that every future machine-assisted question must fail. Separate visible identity candidates are followed by mechanical reconciliation and admission of literal cover identity only. Essential fields retain their inspected source witnesses; optional hidden fields and legal-entity alias inference are excluded. Prior visual review, root literal reading and mechanical reconciliation are distinct roles, not a new visual inspection or agreement study. Author release remains false, and no numerical registry or table entity, period, unit or population binding is admitted. Caption recovery clears the missing-view condition without revising the earlier snapshot."
      ],
      "tables": [
        "semantic"
      ],
      "after_tables": [
        "The next scientific gate is an executable reader on frozen complete evidence, followed by independently authored questions/references and a matched lexical, model-proposal and direct-reader comparison. All arms must see the same acquired evidence; schema validity does not certify question meaning. Natural input fit, missing-evidence controls, complete denominators and residual semantic grading remain necessary. The planned arms receive canonical acquired quantities and therefore test selection and scope, not raw numeric decoding or end-to-end retrieval success.",
        "No retrieval novelty, QA gain, stronger reader, held-out generalization or ACL-ready empirical contribution is established by this checkpoint. The canonical manuscript binds every printed numerical table cell and evidence file hash. Source-bearing artifacts remain external. The PDF uses ReportLab; the editable generic TeX is uncompiled and ACL template compliance is unverified. Earlier manuscripts and failures remain unchanged."
      ]
    }
  ],
